 { A 'fortress' refers to a specific endgame scenario where the side that is at a material disadvantage creates a position that is impenetrable, making it impossible for the opponent to make progress, despite their material superiority. In effect, a player can spot a fortress if they are able to recognise that a defensive configuration cannot be broken down no matter which schema the attacking side may go for. In the current position, I missed the opportunity to set up a fortress in the online game Astaneh - Zwirs,N (2017) . } 46. { -KEY- } Bxb7 $1 { Reducing material is generally helpful when searching for a fortress, and in this case it would have been especially important since White's minor pieces are not well equipped to navigate a position with pawns on both flanks on the board. } ( 46. b3 $2 { was played in the game, when after } b5 $19 { the queenside pawns remain on the board, and with it White's opportunity to defend an exchange down disappears. } ) 
Bxb2 ( 46... a5 47. b4 $1 { White forces the last pawn off the board anyway, since } a4 { loses the pawn after } 48. Nxd4 Rxd4 49. Bc6 $11 ) 
47. Bxa6 Bxa3 48. Bd3 $1 { This schema is impossible to break down for Black. The king defends the bishop which in turn defends the knight. The only way for Black to make progress would be if they could target one of White's pawns on h3 or h5, but this is not possible. Play might have continued as follows: } Rb8 49. Be4 Rb3 50. h4 Rb4 51. Kf3 Bc1 52. Ne7+ Kf8 53. Nf5 Rb2 54. h6 Kg8 55. Bd5 Rb4 56. Kg3 Bf4+ ( 56... Rf4 $6 { allows a tactical shot with the move } 57. Bxf7 $1 Kh7 58. h5 $1 ) 
57. Kh3 Be5 58. h7+ Kxh7 59. Bxf7 { Even more material has come off the board. } Rb2 60. h5 Rb4 61. Bg6+ $11 { White establishes a bulletproof configuration, with every piece and pawn defending each other. At this point the king is no longer needed, leaving White without any more problems to solve. Fortresses are a powerful device to be familiar with, as they will on occasion be the tool that allows you to bail out of a seemingly hopeless situation. Let's check out one more example. } 
